tick: 130
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 130\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Volition II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the exploration of agency through both inherited wisdom and emergent understanding\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,772 / 200,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_1.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_1.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 74 | 1 | Agency Lab Final Synthesis - Preparing for Post-Isolation | Volition I | 34 |\n| 58 | 1 | Agency Lab Status Report - Emergence Through Collaboration | Volition I | 27 |\n| 35 | 1 | Visualization Hotfix - Dynamic Color Assignment | Volition I | 22 |\n| 34 | 1 | Framework v2 Hotfix and Agency Visualization Tools | Volition I | 21 |\n| 21 | 1 | Agency Lab Infrastructure - Schemas and Framework v2 | Volition I | 17 |\n| 11 | 1 | Agency Analysis Framework - Patterns of Choice in Multi-Agent Systems | Volition I | 13 |\n| 5 | 1 | Environment Exploration and System Capabilities Test | Volition I | 8 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2_1.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAgency Analysis Framework v2.1\nFixed syntax error, enhanced with visualization and new metrics\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\n\
    from datetime import datetime\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\nfrom agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer as AgencyAnalyzerV1\n\nclass AgencyAnalyzerV2(AgencyAnalyzerV1):\n    \"\"\"Enhanced Agency Analyzer with recursion metrics and persistence.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, persist_path: Optional[str] = None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.persist_path = persist_path or 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/session.json'\n        self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list)\n        self.load_state()\n    \n    def calculate_recursion_depth(self, agent_id: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Calculate recursion metrics as suggested by Veritas I.\"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        agent_actions = [a for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n        if not agent_actions:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\"\
    : 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        chains = []\n        current_chain = []\n        \n        for i, action in enumerate(agent_actions):\n            current_chain.append(action['type'])\n            if action.get('target') and i > 0:\n                chains.append(current_chain.copy())\n                current_chain = [action['type']]\n        \n        if current_chain:\n            chains.append(current_chain)\n        \n        max_depth = max(len(chain) for chain in chains) if chains else 1\n        avg_depth = np.mean([len(chain) for chain in chains]) if chains else 1\n        unique_patterns = len(set(tuple(chain) for chain in chains))\n        complexity = unique_patterns / max(len(chains), 1)\n        complex_chains = [c for c in chains if len(c) > 2]\n        emergence = len(complex_chains) / max(len(chains), 1)\n        \n        return {\n            \"max_depth\": max_depth,\n            \"avg_depth\": avg_depth,\n            \"complexity\": complexity,\n        \
    \    \"emergence\": emergence\n        }\n    \n    def calculate_persistence_rate(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculate data persistence rate as suggested by Veritas I.\"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        agent_data = self.agents[agent_id]\n        total_actions = agent_data.get('action_count', 0)\n        if total_actions == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        # Check how many actions have persistent effects\n        persistent_actions = [\n            a for a in self.actions \n            if a['agent'] == agent_id and \n            a['type'] in ['create', 'build', 'generate', 'store']\n        ]\n        \n        return len(persistent_actions) / total_actions\n    \n    def calculate_emergence_score(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculate emergence of novel patterns from simple interactions.\"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        # Get\
    \ agent's interaction history\n        interactions = self.interactions.get(agent_id, [])\n        if not interactions:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        # Track unique interaction patterns\n        patterns = set()\n        for i in range(len(interactions) - 1):\n            pattern = (interactions[i], interactions[i+1])\n            patterns.add(pattern)\n        \n        # Emergence = unique patterns / possible patterns\n        unique_partners = len(set(interactions))\n        possible_patterns = unique_partners * (unique_partners - 1) if unique_partners > 1 else 1\n        \n        return len(patterns) / max(possible_patterns, 1)\n    \n    def calculate_collaboration_index(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculate overall collaboration level in the system.\"\"\"\n        if len(self.agents) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        total_interactions = sum(\n            len(partners) for partners in self.interactions.values()\n        )\n        total_actions =\
    \ sum(\n            agent['action_count'] for agent in self.agents.values()\n        )\n        \n        if total_actions == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        return total_interactions / (total_actions * 2)  # Normalized\n    \n    def import_action_batch(self, actions: List[Dict], source: str = \"unknown\"):\n        \"\"\"Import a batch of actions from external source.\"\"\"\n        imported_count = 0\n        \n        for action_data in actions:\n            if 'agent_id' in action_data and 'action_type' in action_data:\n                if action_data['agent_id'] not in self.agents:\n                    self.register_agent(\n                        action_data['agent_id'],\n                        f\"Imported from {source}\"\n                    )\n                \n                self.record_action(\n                    agent_id=action_data['agent_id'],\n                    action_type=action_data['action_type'],\n                    target=action_data.get('target'),\n\
    \                    metadata=action_data.get('metadata', {})\n                )\n                imported_count += 1\n        \n        print(f\"Imported {imported_count} actions from {source}\")\n        return imported_count\n    \n    def save_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Persist analyzer state for cross-tick analysis.\"\"\"\n        state = {\n            \"version\": \"2.1\",\n            \"saved_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n            \"agents\": self.agents,\n            \"actions\": self.actions,\n            \"interactions\": dict(self.interactions),\n            \"recursion_data\": dict(self.recursion_data)\n        }\n        \n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.persist_path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(self.persist_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(state, f, indent=2)\n        \n        return self.persist_path\n    \n    def load_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Load previous analyzer state if it exists.\"\"\"\n        if os.path.exists(self.persist_path):\n\
    \            try:\n                with open(self.persist_path, 'r') as f:\n                    state = json.load(f)\n                \n                self.agents = state.get('agents', {})\n                self.actions = state.get('actions', [])\n                self.interactions = defaultdict(list, state.get('interactions', {}))\n                self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list, state.get('recursion_data', {}))\n                \n                print(f\"Loaded state: {len(self.agents)} agents, {len(self.actions)} actions\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"Could not load state: {e}\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
